## Description

After upgrading to AI SDK v5, I'm encountering an error when trying to use `streamText` without `convertToModelMessages()`, [even though the documentation explicitly states](https://v5.ai-sdk.dev/docs/reference/ai-sdk-ui/convert-to-model-messages#converttomodelmessages:~:text=The%20convertToModelMessages%20function%20is%20no%20longer%20required.%20The%20AI%20SDK%20now%20automatically%20converts%20the%20incoming%20messages%20to%20the%20ModelMessage%20format.):

> The `convertToModelMessages` function is no longer required. The AI SDK now automatically converts the incoming messages to the `ModelMessage` format.

When attempting to use the API without `convertToModelMessages()`:

```plaintext
AI_InvalidPromptError: Invalid prompt: The messages must be a ModelMessage[]. If you have passed a UIMessage[], you can use convertToModelMessages to convert them.
    at (node_modules/.pnpm/ai@5.0.0-beta.25_zod@4.0.5/node_modules/ai/dist/index.mjs:1329:0)
    at (node_modules/.pnpm/ai@5.0.0-beta.25_zod@4.0.5/node_modules/ai/dist/index.mjs:4352:0)
    at (node_modules/.pnpm/ai@5.0.0-beta.25_zod@4.0.5/node_modules/ai/dist/index.mjs:4719:0)
    at (node_modules/.pnpm/ai@5.0.0-beta.25_zod@4.0.5/node_modules/ai/dist/index.mjs:1493:0) {
  name: 'AI_InvalidPromptError',
  cause:  AI_TypeValidationError: Type validation failed: Value: [{"role":"system","parts":[{
  ...
```

### Code Example

Client-side (using `useChat`):

```ts
const useChatResult = useChat({
  transport: new DefaultChatTransport({ api: '/api/chat' }),
  messages: [
    {
      role: 'system',
      parts: [{ type: 'text', text: 'You are a helpful assistant.' }],
      id: 'system-prompt',
    },
    // ... other messages
  ] as UIMessage[],
});
```

Server-side route handler (following v5 docs):

```ts
import { streamText } from 'ai';
import { anthropic } from '@ai-sdk/anthropic';

export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const { messages } = await req.json();

  const result = streamText({
    model: anthropic('claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022'),
    system: 'You are a helpful assistant.',
    messages, // This throws the error
  });

  return result.toUIMessageStreamResponse();
}
```

### Working Solution

The code only works when I explicitly use `convertToModelMessages()`:

```ts
import { convertToModelMessages, streamText } from 'ai';

export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const { messages } = await req.json();

  const modelMessages = convertToModelMessages(messages);

  const result = streamText({
    model: anthropic('claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022'),
    system: 'You are a helpful assistant.',
    messages: modelMessages,
  });

  return result.toUIMessageStreamResponse();
}
```

### Expected Behavior

According to the v5 documentation, the SDK should automatically convert `UIMessage[]` to `ModelMessage[]` format without requiring manual conversion.


## AI SDK Version

- ai: 5.0.0-beta.25
- @ai-sdk/anthropic: 2.0.0-beta.8
- @ai-sdk/react: 2.0.0-beta.25
